# LEVEL 4 - write your .dockerignore here.
#
# When you run "docker build", Docker first SENDS the whole folder (the "build context") to the engine.
# If the folder has big or useless files, the build is slow and the image can get them by accident.
#
# A line in this file = a file or folder that is NOT sent. Example:
#     node_modules/
#     *.tmp
#
# TODO: ignore these things:
#   1. the folder   junk/       (big test files that do not belong to the app)
#   2. all the log files   *.log
#   3. the Dockerfiles themselves   Dockerfile.*
#   4. this file   .dockerignore
